---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Generative Editing"
  description="Paint to fill or remove image regions, or expand a photographic boundary locally in Varve, with reviewable results and an immutable source snapshot."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Generative Editing
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <StatusPill status="experimental" label="Local preview" />
        <h1>Make room in an image without losing the original.</h1>
        <p>
          Paint the pixels that need work, preview a bounded local result, and accept it in the
          existing image layer. Varve's verified local providers handle mask-guided Fill and Remove /
          Generative Subtract in the browser and desktop app. Desktop promptless Expand adds real
          pixels beyond an image while keeping the original exactly in place; browser Expand is
          currently gated after a real-photo visual failure. Prompt-conditioned Replace and Expand
          remain gated until a local model passes compatibility and quality review.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="mode-grid" aria-label="Generative editing modes">
        <article class="mode-card mode-card--available">
          <span class="mode-card__number">01</span>
          <h2>Fill</h2>
          <p>Reconstruct a painted region from the surrounding image context.</p>
          <strong>Available locally</strong>
        </article>
        <article class="mode-card mode-card--available">
          <span class="mode-card__number">02</span>
          <h2>Remove / Generative Subtract</h2>
          <p>Paint over an unwanted object or blemish and rebuild the background without deleting the source layer.</p>
          <strong>Available locally</strong>
        </article>
        <article class="mode-card">
          <span class="mode-card__number">03</span>
          <h2>Replace</h2>
          <p>Prompt-conditioned replacement is wired for desktop, but requires an explicitly imported and qualified local model.</p>
          <strong>Desktop qualification required</strong>
        </article>
        <article class="mode-card mode-card--available">
          <span class="mode-card__number">04</span>
          <h2>Expand</h2>
          <p>Add pixels beyond the current image bounds on desktop. Choose independent sides, a containing aspect ratio or output size, and a side or corner anchor. The retained source is copied through exactly, the full new border including corners is generated, and the result is reviewed before it replaces the image. Browser Expand remains unavailable until a qualified outpainting provider passes visual review.</p>
          <strong>Desktop local · reviewed boundary</strong>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <p class="eyebrow">The workflow</p>
        <h2>Paint, preview, accept.</h2>
        <div class="workflow-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Mark the edit</h3><p>Use a brush, pixel selection, layer mask, image alpha, a Background Removal preview, or a confirmed Object Selection candidate. If you need an automatic mask before painting, Start Object Selection hands control back to the canvas and you can reopen the edit to import the confirmed candidate. The handoff stays disabled when it would discard an in-progress mask. Black preserves the source; white identifies the region to regenerate.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Choose the local path</h3><p>Draft uses the fast PatchMatch path. Higher quality uses the optional LaMa model; prompt-conditioned desktop modes use an explicitly downloaded and validated local diffusion profile. For Fill and Remove / Generative Subtract, only the selected source region is decoded, the working raster is capped for the device tier, and the accepted result remains a bounded patch over the source. Expand builds a validated full-frame plan, protects the retained rectangle byte-for-byte, and states the effective resolution of the generated border.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Review before committing</h3><p>Compare Original and Result, inspect at Fit or 1:1, and keep a generated variation only when it looks right. Reopen an accepted edit and choose Edit mask to refine it without losing the recipe.</p></article>
          <article><span>04</span><h3>Keep the source recoverable</h3><p>Accepting updates the existing image layer in one undoable transaction while retaining an immutable source snapshot and the mask/provider record.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section evidence-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Reviewed on a real photograph</p>
        <h2 id="evidence-title">A promptless local expansion, before and after.</h2>
        <div class="before-after-grid">
          <figure>
            <img
              src={sitePath('/samples/generative-editing/landscape-before.png')}
              alt="Landscape photograph before the image bounds are expanded"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <figcaption>Source photograph · 640px review copy</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img
              src={sitePath('/samples/generative-editing/landscape-after.png')}
              alt="The same landscape photograph with a locally generated right and bottom border"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <figcaption>Promptless Expand · LaMa, desktop local CPU</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p class="evidence-note">
          This reviewed desktop example extends the right and bottom edges without moving or
          rewriting the retained source pixels. The new border is synthesized at a bounded
          resolution and can be softer than the original, so the result remains subject to review
          before acceptance. Browser Expand is currently unavailable because its real-photo Fast
          fallback did not pass visual review.
          Prompt-conditioned Replace and Expand are not represented here because their local model
          qualification is still incomplete.
        </p>
        <p class="evidence-attribution">
          Fixture: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landscape_picture.JPG">“Landscape picture”</a>
          by Michae2109 · public domain. See the <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/generative-editing')}>
          workflow and capability limits</a> for the full qualification boundary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section qualification-section" aria-labelledby="qualification-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Qualification status</p>
        <h2 id="qualification-title">Prompt modes stay gated until they pass.</h2>
        <p class="qualification-note">Varve publishes the verified desktop-local Fill, Remove, and promptless Expand boundary. Promptless Expand was measured on four public-domain photographs: the retained source was byte-identical after composition, generation ran locally in 20 to 60 seconds per image, and the results held for sky, water, grass, studio backdrop, and plain print surround, with a documented architecture limitation. The browser Fast continuation was visually rejected for edge striping and is not offered. The prompt-conditioned model candidates tested on a real photograph did not meet the semantic-quality and runtime-integrity bar, so Replace, prompt-conditioned Fill, and prompt-conditioned Expand remain unavailable. LaMa is not a dedicated outpainting model: the generated border is synthesized at a bounded resolution and detail there is approximate. We do not show an unreviewed before/after as product proof.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section integration-section" aria-labelledby="integration-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Designed to stay in sync</p>
        <h2 id="integration-title">One image workflow, not a detached modal.</h2>
        <div class="integration-grid">
          <p><strong>Reuse existing intent.</strong><br />Start with a brush mask, the current pixel selection, an image layer mask, source alpha, a current Background Removal preview, or a confirmed Object Selection candidate. Expansion, feathering, and bounded context keep the edit aligned to source pixels.</p>
          <p><strong>Keep the document honest.</strong><br />Apply updates the selected image in place, preserves its identity and layout, and retains the original pixels for Restore Original. Provenance, undo, save/reopen, export, and the Layers panel stay on one document state.</p>
          <p><strong>Know what is available.</strong><br />Fill and Remove run locally in the browser and desktop app today. Desktop also exposes promptless Expand within its reviewed photographic boundary. Fast/PatchMatch is the lightweight path for constrained devices, including many Chromebooks and ARM systems; large photographs use a bounded source region and a transparent accepted patch instead of a full inference frame. Desktop Expand copies the retained source through exactly and generates only the new border. Browser Expand, Replace, and prompt-conditioned generation remain gated until a provider passes Varve's compatibility and visual-quality requirements.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <aside class="honesty" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
        <h2 id="privacy-title">Local by default, explicit about limits.</h2>
        <p>
          Current Fill and Remove processing stays on the device in supported browser and desktop
          runtimes; promptless Expand is a desktop-local path. There is no silent cloud fallback.
          The local LaMa model does not read natural-language prompts, so
          prompt text is not treated as conditioning and is not retained in the current local edit
          record. Expanding uploads nothing and costs nothing per attempt. Accepted pixels are
          embedded in the document and render without the model being installed later.
        </p>
        <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/generative-editing')}>Read the workflow guide →</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <a href={sitePath('/download')} class="btn-default">Download Varve</a>
        <a href={sitePath('/features/background-removal')} class="btn-secondary">Explore local image tools</a>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .page-hero h1 { margin: 1rem 0; font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .page-hero p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .mode-grid, .workflow-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); }
  .mode-grid { margin-bottom: 5rem; }
  .mode-card { min-height: 190px; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .mode-card--available { border-color: var(--border-accent); background: var(--surface-accent-soft); }
  .mode-card__number, .workflow-grid span { color: var(--text-tertiary); font: .75rem var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .mode-card h2 { margin: 2.5rem 0 .75rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .mode-card p, .workflow-grid p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; }
  .mode-card strong { display: block; margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .8rem; }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .integration-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 3rem; }
  .integration-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); }
  .integration-grid p { margin: 0; padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  .integration-grid strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .feature-section h2, .honesty h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.8rem; margin: .5rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .workflow-grid article { padding: 1.25rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--border-accent); }
  .workflow-grid h3 { color: var(--text-primary); margin: 1.5rem 0 .5rem; }
  .evidence-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 3rem; }
  .before-after-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); }
  .before-after-grid figure { margin: 0; }
  .before-after-grid img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .before-after-grid figcaption { margin-top: .65rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .evidence-note, .evidence-attribution { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; max-width: 760px; }
  .evidence-attribution { font-size: .9rem; }
  .evidence-attribution a { color: var(--text-link); }
  .qualification-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 3rem; }
  .qualification-note { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; max-width: 760px; }
  .honesty { margin: 2rem 0 3rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding: 1rem 0 1rem 1.25rem; }
  .honesty p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; }
  .honesty a { color: var(--text-link); }
  .feature-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2rem; }
  .btn-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: .7rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-control); color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .integration-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .mode-grid, .workflow-grid, .before-after-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .mode-card { min-height: auto; } .mode-card h2 { margin-top: 1.5rem; } }
</style>
